{"paper": "RRB-GroupD-27-Nov-2025-Shift3.pdf", "status": "ok", "mode": "answer-anchored", "splitter": "qdot", "section_slice": true, "extracted_count": 25, "tagged_count": 22, "questions": [{"n": 1, "text": "Mohan buys a watch for ₹460 and sells it for ₹483. Find his percentage of profit.", "options": [{"text": "5.5%", "added": false}, {"text": "5%", "added": false}, {"text": "4%", "added": false}, {"text": "4.7%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Profit-Loss", "sub": "basic-cp-sp", "key_answer": "5%"}, {"n": 2, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "0", "added": false}, {"text": "2x", "added": false}, {"text": "1", "added": false}, {"text": "x", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Algebra", "sub": "polynomials-and-factorisation", "key_answer": "0"}, {"n": 3, "text": "Anmol and Ayushi together invested ₹46,600 in a business. At the end of the year, out of a total profit of ₹7,500, Anmol's share was ₹2,700. What was Anmol's investment?", "options": [{"text": "₹16,080", "added": false}, {"text": "₹17,240", "added": false}, {"text": "₹16,776", "added": false}, {"text": "₹18,740", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ratio-Proportion", "sub": "partnership", "key_answer": "₹16,776"}, {"n": 4, "text": "A purse contains only ₹5 and ₹10 coins. The total number of coins is 118 and their total value is ₹855. How many coins of ₹5 are there?", "options": [{"text": "53", "added": false}, {"text": "56", "added": false}, {"text": "65", "added": false}, {"text": "55", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Algebra", "sub": "linear-equations", "key_answer": "65"}, {"n": 5, "text": "The average age of 51 students in a class is 24 years. If the age of the teacher is also included, the average age of the whole group becomes 25 years. The age (in years) of the teacher is:", "options": [{"text": "76", "added": false}, {"text": "75", "added": false}, {"text": "77", "added": false}, {"text": "71", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Average", "sub": "series-average", "key_answer": "76"}, {"n": 6, "text": "A, B and C can do a piece of work in 3, 8 and 24 days, respectively. How long (in days) will they take to do thrice the same work, working together?", "options": [{"text": "6", "added": false}, {"text": "18", "added": false}, {"text": "12", "added": false}, {"text": "7", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Work", "sub": "together-apart", "key_answer": "6"}, {"n": 7, "text": "A train P going at the speed of 84 km/hr completely passes train Q of length 447 m, going in the same direction on parallel tracks, at 54 km/hr, in 4.5 minutes. How much time (in seconds) will P take to completely cross train R of length 287 m, going at 87 km/hr in the opposite direction?", "options": [{"text": "36", "added": false}, {"text": "39", "added": false}, {"text": "44", "added": false}, {"text": "34", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Trains", "sub": "two-trains", "key_answer": "44"}, {"n": 8, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "1", "added": false}, {"text": "3", "added": false}, {"text": "0", "added": false}, {"text": "2", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "successive-change", "key_answer": "Increase by 20%"}, {"n": 9, "text": "What is the average of the first 50 even natural numbers?2979", "options": [{"text": "52", "added": false}, {"text": "50", "added": false}, {"text": "54", "added": false}, {"text": "51", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Average", "sub": "simple-average", "key_answer": "51"}, {"n": 10, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "160%", "added": false}, {"text": "165%", "added": false}, {"text": "150%", "added": false}, {"text": "300%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_onl